# AlgoGuard — MAINTAINER-ONLY environment file
#
# This file is a template for credentials that must NEVER ship with the
# analyst package, never be committed with real values, and never be read
# by ordinary application code paths that analysts run.
#
# Copy this to `.env.maintainer` (already covered by .gitignore's `.env.*`
# pattern) and keep it only on trusted maintainer machines. Consumed by
# privileged tooling only: schema migrations, model publishing/training,
# legacy data import, and manual admin/account administration scripts.
# The Flask web app itself must never import this file or its values.

# --- Direct/pooler Postgres connection (maintenance & migrations only) ---
# Use the Supabase connection-pooling string (transaction mode, port 6543),
# not the direct connection — see Stage 5A.1 notes on why.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

# --- Privileged Supabase keys ---
# Full-access key. Bypasses RLS. Server-side/trusted tooling only.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# JWKS endpoint used to verify tokens out-of-band during maintenance/testing.
SUPABASE_JWKS_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/.well-known/jwks.json

# --- Database password (for reference/rotation only; not read by any script) ---
# Store the actual value in a password manager, not here in plaintext for
# long. This line exists only so maintainers know the field is expected
# somewhere in their credential store.
# SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD=

# --- Notes ---
# - Nothing in this file should ever appear in application logs. Any
#   maintainer script that logs a connection string or key must redact it
#   first (see config.py's redaction helper once cloud mode lands in 5D).
# - This file, and any file matching .env.*, is excluded from git and from
#   analyst packaging (Stage 6D.1 removes any privileged path from the
#   analyst distribution entirely).
